    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d153">

                <pb facs="0310" n="206" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg206"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr.
                            Denby</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-10-11"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 11,
                        1890</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 562.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 1151 of the 20th
                    of August last and the copy which you inclose of the last note received from the
                    yamên on the Chi-nan-fu troubles, which, you remark, is simply a repetition of
                    former notes.</p>
                <p>You will, of course, keep the matter in sight and endeavor in all proper ways to
                    further the reasonable desires of Mr. Reid and his associates.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James G. Blaine.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
